<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The table shows the marks of <m>{80}</m> learners in a county mock examination.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Mark</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m>–<m>{19}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m>–<m>{29}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{30}</m>–<m>{39}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{40}</m>–<m>{49}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{50}</m>–<m>{59}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{60}</m>–<m>{69}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (<m>f</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{19}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(a) Find the decile <m>D_{ {2} }</m>, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div><m>D_{ {2} } =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) Find the percentile <m>P_{ {15} }</m>, correct to 1 decimal place.</p><div><m>P_{ {15} } =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>For grouped data the decile <m>D_k</m> is at position <m>kn/10</m> and the percentile <m>P_j</m> at <m>jn/100</m>. Then use the same formula as for quartiles, <m>L + \dfrac{\text{position} - CF}{F} \times c</m>, with <m>L</m> the lower class boundary (the marks are whole numbers, so the class <m>{10}</m>–<m>{19}</m> starts at <m>{9.5}</m>).</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Class</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Frequency (<m>f</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Cumulative frequency (cf)</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m>–<m>{19}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{19}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{19}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m>–<m>{29}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{20}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{39}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{30}</m>–<m>{39}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{15}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{54}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{40}</m>–<m>{49}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{64}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{50}</m>–<m>{59}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{74}</m></cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{60}</m>–<m>{69}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{6}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{80}</m></cell></row></tabular><p>(a) <m>D_{ {2} }</m> is at position <m>{2} \times {80} \div 10 = {16}</m>, in the class <m>{10}</m>–<m>{19}</m>: <me>D_{ {2} } = {9.5} + \frac{ {16} - {0} }{ {19} } \times 10 \approx {17.9}</me></p><p>(b) <m>P_{ {15} }</m> is at position <m>{15} \times {80} \div 100 = {12}</m>, in the class <m>{10}</m>–<m>{19}</m>: <me>P_{ {15} } = {9.5} + \frac{ {12} - {0} }{ {19} } \times 10 \approx {15.8}</me></p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{681}{38}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{601}{38}</m></p></answer>
